    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "c_reference_1",
        "scenarioId": "s_secure",
        "targetKind": "node",
        "targetId": "n_payment",
        "text": "01 | Reference - synchronous payment: Canonical order/owner, transaction outcome and deduplication evidence persist in SQL for the illustrative 90-day period; no raw PAN/CVV, password or reusable token is modeled or stored. Outside SQL, buyer/order context, claims and payment tokens are transient. The callback scenario returns pending to the buyer before the later event; a later user status query is not modeled. These are recommended design controls, not a claim that the synthetic system has been deployed or assessed.",
        "status": "Active",
        "createdAt": 1790969400000,
        "replies": []
      },
      {
        "id": "c_reference_2",
        "scenarioId": "s_risky",
        "targetKind": "node",
        "targetId": "n_payment",
        "text": "02 | Reference - verified callback: Canonical order/owner, transaction outcome and deduplication evidence persist in SQL for the illustrative 90-day period; no raw PAN/CVV, password or reusable token is modeled or stored. Outside SQL, buyer/order context, claims and payment tokens are transient. The callback scenario returns pending to the buyer before the later event; a later user status query is not modeled. These are recommended design controls, not a claim that the synthetic system has been deployed or assessed.",
        "status": "Active",
        "createdAt": 1790969400000,
        "replies": []
      }
    ],
